From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:44:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x86-64: copy at most one eightbyte into each GPR slot

Upstream libffi commits d21881f5 ("Fix x86/ffi64 calls with 6 gp and
some sse registers", #848, libffi 3.4.7) and fe203ffb ("Fix bugs in
the x86-64 and x32 target", #889, libffi 3.4.8), squashed.

ffi_call_int copied the whole argument size into reg_args->gpr[n] for
each INTEGER-class eightbyte. A struct that is split across a GPR and
an SSE register therefore wrote past its GPR slot; when it took the
sixth GPR, the extra bytes landed in the SSE register area and
clobbered arguments already placed there. The first fix copied a fixed
8 bytes, which read past the end of arguments smaller than 8 bytes;
the second bounds the copy to the smaller of the two.
---
 src/x86/ffi64.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/x86/ffi64.c b/src/x86/ffi64.c
index 3bd5273..a8838ff 100644
--- a/src/x86/ffi64.c
+++ b/src/x86/ffi64.c
@@ -650,7 +650,7 @@ ffi_call_int (ffi_cif *cif, void (*fn)(void), void *rvalue,
 		      break;
 		    default:
 		      reg_args->gpr[gprcount] = 0;
-		      memcpy (&reg_args->gpr[gprcount], a, size);
+		      memcpy (&reg_args->gpr[gprcount], a, size <= 8 ? size : 8);
 		    }
 		  gprcount++;
 		  break;
